expression: text
---
Send one round of values, signed with the sensor secret, exactly like a device.
The secret comes from HYDRONODE_SENSOR_SECRET, --secret-stdin, or your login (owner).

Usage: hn push [OPTIONS] <SENSOR> <TYPE=VALUE>...

Arguments:
  <SENSOR>         Sensor id
  <TYPE=VALUE>...  TYPE=VALUE pairs (1 to 64), for example TEMPERATURE=21.4

Options:
      --secret-stdin  Read the sensor secret from stdin
  -h, --help          Print help

Global options:
  -p, --profile <NAME>  Profile to use (server and login), see 'hn profile list'
      --json            Print JSON instead of tables (stable shape, for scripts)

Examples:
  hn push <sensor-id> TEMPERATURE=21.4 HUMIDITY=48
  HYDRONODE_SENSOR_SECRET=… hn push <sensor-id> SOIL_MOISTURE=41
